Add --separate-lora to gRPCServerCLI

LoRA deltas are merged into the model weights at load unless the base is
quantized, bf16 or JIT-offloaded. A merged load bypasses the weights cache,
so an f16 base with a LoRA re-reads the whole checkpoint from disk on every
generation. The app setting that controls this is unreachable from the
server, which builds an empty settings workspace in a fresh temp dir at
every start. The flag sets ModelZoo.isSeparateLoRAPreferred, which
isQuantizedModel reads, and all fourteen decision sites go through that
function. LoHa still merges, because there is no separate path for it.
